## 5. Insights

- `spr.v5.b32`: 82% of the scalar add peak, 20% of the SIMD peak, 22% of the roofline (geomean). 2/20 points sit left of the ridge (DRAM-bound roof).
  - Far below every ceiling: neither DRAM bandwidth nor the add units are the limit. The time goes into latency: index loads, gathers, short loops with data-dependent trip counts (branch mispredicts).
  - ns/add rises strongly with k in 15/20 cases: larger k saves additions but each one costs more.
- `spr.v6.b32`: 79% of the scalar add peak, 20% of the SIMD peak, 21% of the roofline (geomean). 2/20 points sit left of the ridge (DRAM-bound roof).
  - Far below every ceiling: neither DRAM bandwidth nor the add units are the limit. The time goes into latency: index loads, gathers, short loops with data-dependent trip counts (branch mispredicts).
  - ns/add rises strongly with k in 15/20 cases: larger k saves additions but each one costs more.

